! ======================================================================
! test_v1101_h2_tdhf_rt_kick -- RT-TDDFT ladder step 3, the two-road
! oracle at full exact exchange: the weak-kick RT spectrum of H2 must
! reproduce the Casida (full TDHF/RPA) excitation energy AND oscillator
! strength.  c_HF = 1 exercises the complete complex-exchange machinery
! (K[Im P] via the general stored contraction) on every step.
!
! H2/STO-3G, R = 0.74 A: one singlet excitation (sigma_u, z-polarized).
! Kick kappa = 1e-3 along z; 12000 steps of dt = 0.1 (T = 1200 au),
! gamma = 0.005 (gamma*T = 6).
!
! Reference (v1.10.1, 1 thread, reference BLAS):
!   SCF total energy:            -1.116780126821
!   RT self-check |dE|:           ~4e-16
!   Casida (printed above the RT section):
!     state 1:  w = 0.930653 Ha (25.3244 eV),  f = 0.88575
!   RT excitation table:
!     state:    w = 0.93119  Ha (25.3389 eV),  f = 0.886151
!   Agreement: dw = +5.4e-4 Ha, df = +0.05 %.
!   The position residual is the O(w^3 dt^2) propagator PHASE error,
!   verified by its exact dt^2 scaling (dt = 0.2 gives dw = +2.2e-3 =
!   4x); the two flanking "(ringing?)"-flagged satellites are finite-
!   trajectory truncation lobes at the exp(-gamma*T) level, correctly
!   labeled by the analyzer.
!   Post-kick energy conservation: max |E(t)-E(0)| ~ 2.4e-11 Ha over
!   12000 steps -- with exact exchange this is a stringent implicit
!   test of K[Im P] (an inconsistent antisymmetric exchange breaks
!   conservation immediately).
!   Kick-amplitude linearity: kappa = 1e-4 changes f by 5e-5 relative
!   (the O(kappa^2) nonlinearity), positions unchanged.
! ======================================================================
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%scf_ptol 1e-9
%tddft   3
%rt_tddft 12000
%rt_dt    0.1
%rt_kick  0.001
%rt_kick_dir z
%rt_gamma 0.005
%rt_print_every 3000
%geom angstrom
H  0.0 0.0 0.0
H  0.0 0.0 0.74
*end
